@page "/terms"
@layout LegalLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

@using Akinai.Shared.Billing
@using Akinai.Shared.Api.Billing
@inject ICall<GetPlans, List<PlanDefinition>> GetPlansCall

<PageTitle>Terms and Conditions — Akinai</PageTitle>

<h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
<p class="lgupdated">Last updated @LastUpdated</p>

<p class="lgintro">
    These terms cover your use of Akinai. By creating an account you agree to them.
    We have tried to write them in plain language — where something matters to your
    money or your data, it is called out rather than buried.
</p>

<h2>1. The service</h2>
<p>
    Akinai is software for creating, sending and tracking invoices and estimates,
    recording time and expenses, and reconciling payments. We provide the tool. The
    contents of anything you send — the amounts, the tax treatment, the terms you
    offer — are yours.
</p>

<div class="lgnote">
    <p>
        <strong>We are not your accountant.</strong> Akinai does not give tax, legal
        or financial advice, and does not check whether an invoice is correct or
        compliant where you or your client are based. Tax rates, invoice numbering
        rules and mandatory fields vary by country and change over time. Getting
        those right is your responsibility, and we would encourage you to have a
        local accountant confirm your setup.
    </p>
</div>

<h2>2. Your account</h2>
<p>
    You need an account to use Akinai. You must give an accurate email address,
    keep your credentials secure, and take responsibility for what happens under
    your account. Tell us promptly if you think someone else has access to it.
</p>
<p>
    Accounts are for a single business or individual. You may not share one set of
    credentials across several people as a way of avoiding subscription costs.
</p>

<h2>3. Plans and pricing</h2>
<p>
    Akinai has a free plan and a paid plan. Current prices:
</p>

<div class="lgtable-wrap">
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr><th>Plan</th><th>Monthly</th><th>Annual</th><th>Main limits</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var plan in _plans)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>@plan.Name</strong></td>
                    <td>@(plan.IsPaid ? $"{plan.CurrencySymbol}{plan.MonthlyPrice:0.##}" : "Free")</td>
                    <td>@(plan.IsPaid ? $"{plan.CurrencySymbol}{plan.AnnualPrice:0.##}" : "Free")</td>
                    <td>
                        @(plan.InvoicesPerMonth is int limit
                            ? $"{limit} invoices per month"
                            : "Unlimited invoices")@(plan.AllLanguages ? ", all languages" : ", English only")@(plan.MultiCurrency ? ", multi-currency" : ", one currency")
                    </td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<p>
    Prices are in @Currency and exclude any sales tax or VAT, which is calculated
    and shown at checkout based on where you are. We may change prices, but not for
    a period you have already paid for — we will give you at least 30 days' notice
    by email before a change affects your renewal.
</p>

<h2>4. Subscriptions, renewal and cancellation</h2>

<h3>Renewal is automatic</h3>
<p>
    A paid subscription renews by itself at the end of each billing period — monthly
    or annually, whichever you chose — and your saved payment method is charged
    automatically. We will notify you in the app each time a renewal is taken.
</p>

<h3>Cancelling</h3>
<div class="lgnote">
    <p>
        <strong>Cancelling does not cut you off immediately, and does not refund the
        current period.</strong> When you cancel, your plan stays active until the
        end of the period you have already paid for, then moves to the Free plan.
        Nothing you have created is deleted.
    </p>
</div>

<h3>If a payment fails</h3>
<p>
    If a renewal payment is declined, your account moves to Free plan limits until
    payment succeeds. Your data stays intact — you keep access to everything you
    have created, but paid features stop until you update your payment method.
</p>

<h3>Refunds</h3>
<p>
    We do not offer refunds for partial periods. If something has gone genuinely
    wrong — you were charged twice, or billed after cancelling — email us and we
    will put it right. Where you have a statutory right to cancel or to a refund
    under your local consumer law, that right stands regardless of anything here.
</p>

<h2>5. What happens to your data if you downgrade</h2>
<p>
    Moving from Pro to Free never deletes anything. Invoices, estimates, clients and
    time entries all remain. What changes is what you can do next: features not
    included in Free stop being available, and the monthly invoice limit applies to
    new invoices. Documents you already sent remain valid and your clients can still
    open the links you shared.
</p>

<h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
<p>You agree not to use Akinai to:</p>
<ul>
    <li>send invoices for goods or services you have not provided, or that are fraudulent</li>
    <li>break the law where you or your client are based, including sanctions and anti-money-laundering rules</li>
    <li>send unsolicited bulk email through the service</li>
    <li>attempt to gain access to another account, or to disrupt or probe the service</li>
    <li>resell or white-label Akinai as your own product without a written agreement</li>
</ul>
<p>
    We may suspend or close an account that breaches this section. Where we can, we
    will tell you first and give you a chance to put it right.
</p>

<h2>7. Translation and automated features</h2>
<p>
    Akinai translates the text you write on a document into your client's language
    using a machine translation service. The document's fixed headings are
    professionally set per language; the text you wrote is machine-translated.
</p>
<div class="lgnote">
    <p>
        <strong>Machine translation is not a legal translation.</strong> Review
        anything that carries obligations — payment terms, scope of work, penalty
        clauses — before you send it. If a translated term and your original differ
        in meaning, that is a difference your client may rely on. Translation is
        subject to a monthly allowance on your plan; once it is used up, documents
        render in the original text rather than failing.
    </p>
</div>

<h2>8. Availability</h2>
<p>
    We work to keep Akinai available and to protect your data, but we do not
    guarantee uninterrupted service. We may take it down for maintenance, and
    features may change. If we plan an interruption that would affect you
    materially, we will give notice where practical.
</p>
<p>
    Keep your own copies of anything you cannot afford to lose. You can export your
    data at any time from Account → Personal data.
</p>

<h2>9. Liability</h2>
<p>
    Akinai is provided as-is. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for
    lost profits, lost business, or indirect or consequential loss, and our total
    liability to you in any twelve-month period is limited to what you paid us in
    that period.
</p>
<p>
    Nothing here limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence,
    for fraud, or for anything else that cannot lawfully be limited. If you are a
    consumer, your statutory rights are unaffected.
</p>

<h2>10. Ending the agreement</h2>
<p>
    You may stop using Akinai and delete your account at any time. We may end this
    agreement if you materially breach these terms, or if we discontinue the
    service — in which case we will give you reasonable notice and time to export
    your data.
</p>

<h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
<p>
    We may update these terms. If a change materially affects your rights, we will
    give notice by email or in the app before it takes effect, and continuing to use
    Akinai after that means you accept the updated terms.
</p>

<h2>12. Governing law</h2>
<p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales, and the courts of
    England and Wales have non-exclusive jurisdiction. If you are a consumer
    resident elsewhere, you keep the protection of the mandatory consumer laws where
    you live, and may bring proceedings there.
</p>

<h2>13. Contact</h2>
<p>
    Questions about these terms go to
    <a href="mailto:@ContactEmail">@ContactEmail</a>, or use the
    <a href="contact">contact page</a>.
</p>

@code {
    private const string LastUpdated = "24 July 2026";
    private const string ContactEmail = "hello@akinaiapp.com";

    // Prices come from the live catalogue for the same reason the landing page
    // does it: a terms page quoting a price the checkout does not charge is
    // worse than no table at all. Falls back to the compiled defaults.
    private IReadOnlyList<PlanDefinition> _plans = Plans.All;

    private string Currency => _plans.FirstOrDefault()?.Currency ?? "GBP";

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        var plans = await GetPlansCall.Call(new GetPlans());
        if (plans is { Count: > 0 }) _plans = plans;
    }
}
